    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.optimize_graph_edit_distance - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.optimize_graph_edit_distance.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.optimize_graph_edit_distance()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Iterate over improving estimates of the exact graph edit distance.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.optimize_graph_edit_distance()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Iterate over improving estimates of the exact graph edit distance.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.optimize_graph_edit_distance()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n  .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Iterate over improving estimates of the exact graph edit distance.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nIterate over improving estimates of the exact graph edit distance.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L52107-L52233){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.optimize_graph_edit_distance(\n    other,\n    node_match=None,\n    edge_match=None,\n    node_subst_cost=None,\n    node_del_cost=None,\n    node_ins_cost=None,\n    edge_subst_cost=None,\n    edge_del_cost=None,\n    edge_ins_cost=None,\n    upper_bound=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Improving edit distance estimates](../assets/graphs/optimize-graph-edit-distance.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Graph G is a diamond, two triangles sharing edge A–B; H is the same diamond on other labels, sharing D–E, with an extra node B hanging off E (accent). The search yields the costs 10, 8, 6 and 4 as it finds cheaper edit paths, and ends at 2, the exact distance: insert node B and edge E–B.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe exact search behind `graph_edit_distance(exact=True)` finds complete edit paths of\nstrictly decreasing cost until no cheaper one exists. This method yields each of those\ncosts in turn, so the last value is the exact graph edit distance and every earlier one\nis an upper bound on it.\n\nUse it to:\n\n- stop early with a good-enough distance, by breaking out of the loop\n- follow how quickly the search converges on a pair of graphs\n\nThe whole search runs before the first value is yielded, so breaking out early saves no\ntime; pass `upper_bound=` to `graph_edit_distance()`, or `timeout=` to it or to\n`optimize_edit_paths()`, to cap the work instead. Parameters are as in\n`optimal_edit_paths()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[other]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The target graph. It must have the same directedness as the calling graph.\n\n<code>[node_match]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], bool]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Functions called with two attribute dictionaries, returning `True` when the two may\n    be substituted for free. See `graph_edit_distance()`.\n\n<code>[edge_match]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], bool]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Functions called with two attribute dictionaries, returning `True` when the two may\n    be substituted for free. See `graph_edit_distance()`.\n\n<code>[node_subst_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Functions returning the cost of substituting, deleting, and inserting a node.\n\n<code>[node_del_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Functions returning the cost of substituting, deleting, and inserting a node.\n\n<code>[node_ins_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Functions returning the cost of substituting, deleting, and inserting a node.\n\n<code>[edge_subst_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The same three functions for edges.\n\n<code>[edge_del_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The same three functions for edges.\n\n<code>[edge_ins_cost]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable[[dict, dict], float]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The same three functions for edges.\n\n<code>[upper_bound]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The largest cost to consider. Only costs up to this value are yielded.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Iterator[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The costs of successively cheaper edit paths, ending with the edit distance.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graphs differ in directedness, or a cost is negative or not a number.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~graph_edit_distance`) \n\n:   The final value directly.\n\n[](`~optimize_edit_paths`) \n\n:   The same search, yielding the edit paths too.\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nMatches NetworkX's `optimize_graph_edit_distance()` in its final value. The intermediate\nvalues depend on the order in which equally good assignments are explored, so they can\ndiffer from NetworkX's.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe estimates for a six-node cycle and a seven-node wheel end at the exact distance,\n`7.0`:\n\n::: {#03aa10aa .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ncycle = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(6)\nwheel = ec.Graph().add_wheel_graph(7)\n\nlist(cycle.optimize_graph_edit_distance(wheel))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[7.0]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### How far caffeine is from benzene\n\nCaffeine has 14 atoms and 15 bonds, and benzene is a ring of 6 carbons. By shape alone,\nthe search settles at 17, deleting 8 atoms and 9 bonds around caffeine's ring of six:\n\n::: {#80412f02 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmolecules = ec.molecules()\ncaffeine, benzene = molecules[\"caffeine\"], molecules[\"benzene\"]\n\nlist(caffeine.optimize_graph_edit_distance(benzene))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n[21.0, 19.0, 17.0]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWith elements matched, the search takes longer to converge and ends 2 higher, at 19:\ntwo atoms of caffeine's ring are nitrogens, and substituting them for benzene's carbons\ncosts 1 each:\n\n::: {#14753ec9 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ndef same_element(x, y):\n    return x[\"element\"] == y[\"element\"]\n\n\nlist(caffeine.optimize_graph_edit_distance(benzene, node_match=same_element))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n[27.0, 26.0, 24.0, 23.0, 22.0, 21.0, 19.0]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#c5c71223 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nring = list(caffeine.subgraph_isomorphisms(benzene, limit=1)[0].values())\n\ncaffeine.plot(color_by=\"element\", highlight=ring + ring[:1], label_by=\"label\", seed=1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light,